The uncorrected coincidence probabilities of FMS \(\pi^{0}\) - BEMC \(\pi^{0}\) azimuthal correlations in p+p and d+Au collisions are shown in Figure 4.7. To characterize the azimuthal correlations, results are fitted with a function \(G(x)\) which is a constant plus a Gaussian function. The constant is to fit the background related with non-correlation part and the Gaussian function is to fit the peak of the correlation,

